reason: "Investigated and confirmed the toggle itself is not broken: the checkbox's (change) handler passes movie.id from the rendered row into toggleWatched, and onRowClick's closest('a, button, input') check makes the same click a no-op on the row handler, so the clicked movie toggles exactly once (the test's own watchedCount()===1 and '1 of 2 watched' assertions at lines 50-51 would pass). It fails at line 49 because the checkbox() helper always reads the checkbox at display position 0: under the round-1 sorted display (every unwatched item before every watched item) the newly watched Movie 1 is re-sorted to the last row, so display position 0 is now the unwatched Movie 2, whose checkbox is unchecked - hence 'expected false to be true'. The assertion only holds under the old unsorted display order where the toggled movie stayed at position 0, so this test cannot pass while keeping the mandated sorted display. Not editing it per instruction; requesting approval to update it to locate the clicked movie's checkbox by id/title instead of display position (the behaviour is pinned by the new passing regression tests added in this submission)."

